{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Eleven days from Horev.</b> Moses said to them: See what you caused yourselves. There is no shorter route from Horev to Kadesh Barnea than by way of Mount Se'ir, and even that is a journey of eleven days — yet you traveled it in three days. For on the twentieth of Iyyar they set out from Horev, as it says (Numbers 10) ״וַיְהִי בַּשָּׁנָה הַשֵּׁנִית בַּחֹדֶשׁ הַשֵּׁנִי בְּעֶשְׂרִים בַּחֹדֶשׁ וְגוֹ׳״, and on the twenty-ninth of Sivan they sent the spies from Kadesh Barnea (Ta'anit 29). Subtract from them the thirty days they spent at Kivrot HaTa'avah, where they ate the meat a month of days, and the seven days they spent at Hatzerot for Miriam to be confined there — it turns out that in three days they traversed that entire route. And all the while the Shekhinah was exerting itself for your sake to hasten your entry into the land. But because you spoiled, He turned you around the environs of Mount Se'ir forty years (see Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:22.617698051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}